# Husky Initialization

Husky initialization is determined by the presence of this specific file. If the file exists, it triggers the initialization of Husky, as defined in the `postinstall` script in `package.json`:

```
  "postinstall": "test -f .hi && (is-ci || husky) || true"
```

This script ensures that:
 - Husky is only initialized when working directly within the package’s own repository.
   - When this package is used as a dependency in another project, this file will not be included in the package contents preventing Husky from being set up.
 - If the environment is a CI/CD pipeline, Husky is skipped automatically, thanks to the is-ci package, which detects CI environments and prevents unnecessary Git hooks from running.

This setup ensures a clean and efficient workflow without unwanted Git hooks in CI or external projects.

 - [husky documentation](https://typicode.github.io/husky/)
 - [is-ci hocumentation](https://www.npmjs.com/package/is-ci)
